# Frontend — components

Build replaceable pieces, not page monoliths.

| Level | Where | Examples |
|-------|--------|----------|
| **Primitives** | `components/ui/` | Button, Field |
| **Sections** | `components/home/<section>/` | Hero, Projects |
| **Pages** | `app/` | Compose only |

Promote to `components/ui/` only when used in **2+** places.

- One component, one job. Split presentational UI from state when state grows
- Props in, events out
- UI copy comes from `messages[locale]` inside `LocalePanels`. No hardcoded sentences, no next-intl
- Colocate a hook next to its component. Shared helpers go in `lib/`
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default
- Lists use stable `key`s (ids, not indexes)
- Images are sized. No layout shift. No JS animation library
- Tokens live in the Tailwind theme, not scattered hex in JSX
- Client components only where the page reacts. A locale switch is a button and does not change the URL. The lead form is a plain HTML form

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — 400-line page with prices inlined in markup
// ✅ GOOD — <ServiceList items={services} />; page only stacks sections
```
